---
title: Pairing a Solo reader
sidebar:
  order: 4
---

In order to initiate a payment on a Solo device using [Cloud API](/terminal-payments/tools/cloud-api), the device must be enrolled with the Merchant account. This enrollment process is what we call a Reader Pairing.

The pairing process starts on the device side by generating the pairing code.

{% aside type="note"%}
The pairing process has an expiration time of 5 minutes, if any issue occurs, the whole process must be restarted.
{% /aside %}

## Generating the Pairing Code

#### 1. Turn on the Reader

{% aside type="note"%}
Do not log in to the Solo reader. The pairing process will be done via the Cloud API.
{% /aside %}

{% soloscreen src="/img/guides/solo-pairing-step-1.png" alt="Solo device login screen." /%}

##### 2. Open the menu drawer

{% soloscreen src="/img/guides/solo-pairing-step-2.png" alt="Solo device menu drawer." /%}

##### 3. Go to Connections

{% soloscreen src="/img/guides/solo-pairing-step-4.png" alt="Solo device connection settings." /%}

##### 4. Select API

{% soloscreen src="/img/guides/solo-pairing-step-5.png" alt="Solo device API pairing initiation screen." /%}

##### 5. Tap on Connect

{% soloscreen src="/img/guides/solo-pairing-step-6.png" alt="Solo device API pairing code screen." /%}

With the pairing code, proceed with [Pair the Reader to the Merchant Account](#pair-the-reader-to-the-merchant-account).

## Pair the Reader to the Merchant Account

{% aside type="note"%}
For a full list of the available parameters, see the [API Reference](/api/readers/create-reader).
{% /aside %}

{% tabs %}
{% tabitem label="cURL"%}
```bash
curl -X POST \
  https://api.sumup.com/v0.1/merchants/{merchant_code}/readers \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer $SUMUP_API_KEY' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{
        "pairing_code": "918MPQHZ"
      }'
```
{% /tabitem %}
{% /tabs %}

The response contains a JSON body with the details of the created reader resource. What you need to note in the response is the identifier of the resource - you will need it for all operations that you perform with the resource.

```json
{
  "id": "rdr_3MSAFM23CK82VSTT4BN6RWSQ65",
  "name": "Frontdesk",
  "status": "processing",
  "device": {
    "identifier": "200100010001",
    "model": "solo"
  },
  "created_at": "2023-05-09T14:50:20.214Z",
  "updated_at": "2023-05-09T14:52:58.714Z"
}
```

### Wait for Confirmation

If the client successfully performed the previous steps, the device will show a confirmation screen:

{% soloscreen src="/img/guides/solo-pairing-step-7.png" alt="Solo device API pairing confirmation screen." /%}

and transit to the Idle Screen:

{% soloscreen src="/img/guides/solo-pairing-step-8.png" alt="Solo device idle screen." /%}

# Unpairing a Solo reader

In order to unpair a reader from the merchant account, two steps are required:

1. [Unlink Reader](#unlink-reader) from the Merchant account (via Readers API);
2. [Disconnect Reader](#diconnect-reader) (manually via Solo)

### Unlink Reader

{% aside type="note"%}
For a full list of the available parameters, see the [API Reference](/api/readers/delete-reader).
{% /aside %}

{% tabs %}
{% tabitem label="cURL"%}
```bash
curl -X DELETE \
  https://api.sumup.com/v0.1/merchants/{merchant_code}/readers/{id} \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer $SUMUP_API_KEY'
```
{% /tabitem %}
{% /tabs %}

### Diconnect Reader

##### 1. Open the menu drawer

{% soloscreen src="/img/guides/solo-unpairing-step-1.png" alt="Solo device menu drawer." /%}

##### 2. Go to Connections

{% soloscreen src="/img/guides/solo-unpairing-step-2.png" alt="Solo device connection settings." /%}

##### 3. Select API

{% soloscreen src="/img/guides/solo-unpairing-step-3.png" alt="Solo device active API connection screen." /%}

##### 4. Tap on Disconnect

Your Solo device is now disconnected.

